{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470029-maximum-feats-of-strength-for-a-neonate-new-character","id":1470029,"title":"Maximum feats of strength for a Neonate (new character) ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-09T06:37:13-08:00","id":1470029,"title":"Maximum feats of strength for a Neonate (new character) ?","content":"Let's take a newbie vampire ( new character ) with Potence 5 ( 3 base + 2 dots bought for 14 character points ) who pumps his Strength to 9 by spending Blood Points, with base Strength 4 or 5 who gives access to an appropriate Specialization ( weight lifting / weight throwing / breaking things ecc. ), the Giant physical merit ( bought with flaws, who gives some unspecified bonus to feats of strength ) and some technique in lifting / breaking / throwing things ( 3 dots in Athletics ). Needless to say, he's trying very hard ( Willpower expenditure ). And is really, really angry to boot ( berserker merit, Frenzy )<br /> <br /> So: Strength 9 + strength specialization + Potence 5 + Athletics 3 + Giant + Willpower expenditure + Frenzy.<br /> <br /> What can he break / lift / throw, more or less, in your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T13:41:33-08:00","id":1470071,"title":"","content":"This is under the assumption you are playing V20, if you are playing an older edition disregard what I am about to type:<br /> <br /> In terms of lifting things, only <b>Strength</b> applies and is only rolled in teamwork situations it seems. That said, let's assume you pump your Strength to 10 with blood, which you can do in V20, and you have 5 Potence. You would have 15 strength, which is literally the highest possibility on the V20 <b>Feats of Strength</b> chart, and it allows you to lift around 2720 kg (6000 lbs.) of weight and <b>Throw a truck</b> is listed as the example for that level of Strength.<br /> <br /> Now to actually throw something you need to roll a <b>Dexterity + Athletics</b> after lifting the thing. So 3 Athletics and a decent Dex is enough to throw a fucking truck at an unfortunate group of kine.<br /> <br /> Breaking things also seems to be automatic, although how it's handled is vague. Ultimately at 15 Strength, you're basically strong enough to rip a truck in half with ease. If you were to roll, you'd likely be able to severally dent part of a steel beam supporting a building.<br /> <br /> <b>Athletics </b>is not used in lifting or breaking objects, so it doesn't factor at all for lifting per say. Giant, Huge Size merit, also doesn't apply outside of pushing objects it seems. The Willpower spending is not needed, and Frenzy adds nothing to this situation outside of not suffering wound penalties. Also the Specialization would likely not apply outside of damage to objects, which would be devastating BTW.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, you can lift a truck with ease. Not only that, but will a powerful Willpower roll (Difficulty 9), you might be able to do a hell of a lot worse, like take out a building,<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T14:03:53-08:00","id":1470075,"title":"","content":"So, capture and keep prisoner a vampire, even a Neonate, could very well be pratically impossible...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T14:33:42-08:00","id":1470076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470029-maximum-feats-of-strength-for-a-neonate-new-character?p=1470075#post1470075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, capture and keep prisoner a vampire, even a Neonate, could very well be pratically impossible...</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Just cut their arms and legs off?<br /> <br /> More seriously, severly limiting the amount of blood they have access to will prevent rediculous strength spiking (and healing their limbs back if you want to be extra careful. Ideally cut off with agg or Vis and not letting your captive have enough rest to heal will also prevent them regenerating)<br /> <br /> Assuming just keeping them staked isn't an option for whatever reason...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T19:25:08-08:00","id":1470102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470029-maximum-feats-of-strength-for-a-neonate-new-character?p=1470075#post1470075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, capture and keep prisoner a vampire, even a Neonate, could very well be pratically impossible...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually no. Most Cainites will not do this, or even know they can. The reason why is it needs a massive quantity of blood to do the extreme scenario I proposed. The average neonates has around 2 Strength and maybe 1 potence. With this in mind it would take anywhere between 1 to 4 points of blood to break restraints. That's can be as much as 40% or even 50% of their supply. This would make the vampire a sitting duck if the hunters are smart about it.<br /> <br /> Btw breaking restraints needs 4 to 7 Strength depending on the quality of the restraints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T06:06:55-08:00","id":1470122,"title":"","content":"I read that a thick chain ( 1/2 inches, 236 lbs for 100 feet ) can hold up to 12.000 lbs. So, you can wrap it around the vampire approximately 4 or 5 times, and the pressure needed to break it would become something around 50.000 lbs. <br /> You would need a thick pillar to attach the chain, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T09:41:32-08:00","id":1470149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470029-maximum-feats-of-strength-for-a-neonate-new-character?p=1470122#post1470122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read that a thick chain ( 1/2 inches, 236 lbs for 100 feet ) can hold up to 12.000 lbs. So, you can wrap it around the vampire approximately 4 or 5 times, and the pressure needed to break it would become something around 50.000 lbs. <br /> You would need a thick pillar to attach the chain, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd also need a person with above average strength to wrap it. Hunters tend to range so for some that kind of restraint is ideal. However I just remember the Hunter's best strat, wait until dawn. It's the main reason Elders have so many safety nets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T12:37:25-08:00","id":1470363,"title":"","content":"I've never fully understood the Feat of strength in the world of darkness. The chart get to 15 strength point to mesure the possible action of a character, but as a player of the v20 books i know that a vampire with fives dots in strength + 5 dots in potency are able to get to 10 in the chart. They can spend blood points to get to 15 for a short period.<br /> In other books like Werewolf, with 5 dots in strength and with the +4 of the crinos form they can get to 9 in the chart but the feat of strength can provide them only 5 dots of strength, so they get to 14.... on a chart that go to 15....<br /> To my knowledge there's 2 or 3 gifts that allows them to increase their strength, and they're high ranks so for the majority of the player they can get to 14 only with a lucky roll<br /> There's missing 1 point to get to 15 &quot;as easily&quot; as a vampire with the good powers.<br /> In addition the chart of the v20 books mention a &quot;dice pool&quot; for the feats of strength, it confuse us","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T16:42:33-08:00","id":1470387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470029-maximum-feats-of-strength-for-a-neonate-new-character?p=1470363#post1470363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's missing 1 point to get to 15 &quot;as easily&quot; as a vampire with the good powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's the wrong comparison. You're comparing a base werewolf with an optimized vampire in an optimized situation unlikely to actually come into play.<br /> <br /> The common Werewolf gets +4 to Str on Crinos. The common vampire gets... the ability to waste Blood for barely the same effect? The starting vampire can bump blood to get to Str 6 for a scene, but that costs as much as they already miss from 6. And as popular as it is, Potence isn't something even most neonates have. You can expect the average Neonate to have 1 or 2 at their In-Clans and frequently not have all their In-Clans, so Potence s a possibility, not something to expect. Much less at 5.<br /> <br /> And while this is possible for a starting character, at what cost? What else can the werewolf get if they decide to be as focused as this character on the starting sheet?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27051_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27051\" data-vbnamecard=\"27051\">Solomon Draak</a> holding down any vampire with full blood and health, without hindering their actions in any way should be indeed near impossible for mortals. For the entirety of three rounds, at least, the duration of any buff beyond your Generational Limit +1. Then a single scene for the rest. But keep in mind the cost and time for the effort, not to mention how unlikely this particular set of stats is. If you know your target and play smart, it can be a lot easier (or, on the other hand, you can be duped by a target that actually knows you and your plans).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}